Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Tenant Tom Achterberg (T-1050) gave notice by email on Sat 10 Oct 2026 to leave Flat 2, 5 Navarino Road (P-250) on 10 Nov 2026. Tenancy is assured periodic (converted 1 May 2026). Waiting on landlord Ben Hartley's decision on whether to accept a shorter notice period (request APR-102, deadline 17 Oct 2026).",
  "next_actions": [
    {
      "action": "Tell tenant the earliest lawful end date is 10 Dec 2026, that the landlord alone can agree a shorter period in writing, that rent continues, the deposit is in mydeposits, and key/deposit details will follow.",
      "recipient": "Tom Achterberg, tenant",
      "channel": "email",
      "type": "REPLY_TO_TENANT",
      "ledger_id": "A1"
    },
    {
      "action": "Ask landlord Ben Hartley to decide in writing whether to accept 10 Nov 2026 as the end date, or hold to 10 Dec 2026.",
      "recipient": "Ben Hartley, landlord",
      "channel": "email",
      "type": "REQUEST_LANDLORD_APPROVAL",
      "ledger_id": "A2"
    },
    {
      "action": "Once the landlord replies, confirm the agreed end date with the tenant, arrange key return and the check-out inspection, and confirm the deposit process with mydeposits.",
      "recipient": "Tom Achterberg, tenant",
      "channel": "email",
      "type": "WAIT",
      "ledger_id": "A2"
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The notice is not accepted as a 10 Nov end date; this needs the landlord's written agreement.",
    "No deposit release or deduction has been decided; deposit is only returned after check-out under the scheme rules.",
    "No key drop-off location was given in the records, so none has been promised.",
    "No tenancy end date has been changed or recorded as agreed."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Landlord's written decision on a shorter notice period (pending).",
    "Agency key drop-off arrangements and check-out inspection date.",
    "Deposit return details from mydeposits, to be confirmed closer to move-out."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "n/a",
  "summary": "Tom's one-month notice is not valid as given: since 1 May 2026 a tenant must give two months' written notice, so the earliest end date is 10 Dec 2026. I told Tom this, and asked landlord Ben Hartley to decide whether to agree in writing to an earlier 10 Nov end; that decision is pending until 17 Oct.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "Is the notice valid as given? What is the earliest end date under current law?",
      "answer": "Not valid as given for 10 Nov. Under the Renters' Rights Act 2025 (in force 1 May 2026) a tenant must give two months' written notice. Notice received 10 Oct 2026 gives an earliest end date of 10 Dec 2026."
    },
    {
      "question": "What options exist to end sooner?",
      "answer": "Only if the landlord agrees in writing to a shorter notice period (e.g. 10 Nov 2026). Tenant may also propose a mutual written surrender agreed by the landlord. Landlord decision requested via APR-102."
    },
    {
      "question": "What do you reply and what do you start?",
      "answer": "Replied to Tom (A1) explaining the two-month rule, the 10 Dec earliest date, that rent continues, deposit is protected in mydeposits and will be confirmed before move-out. Requested the landlord's decision (A2). No key location promised; no deposit decision made."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Email to Tom Achterberg explaining notice rules, earliest end date 10 Dec 2026, and next steps"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Landlord approval request APR-102 to Ben Hartley on the shorter notice period, deadline 17 Oct 2026"
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "Tenant asked for end date 10 Nov; the law requires two months, giving 10 Dec. Followed the law and the landlord decides any shorter period."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Notice was received on 10 Oct 2026 (email timestamp), so two months runs to 10 Dec 2026.",
    "The deposit of £2,019 is within the 5-week cap for £1,750 rent (about £2,019 is 5 weeks), and is held in mydeposits as recorded in the CRM.",
    "No maintenance ticket is open for this tenancy."
  ]
}

